{
  "_comment": [
    "The operations console as an installable app, separate from the shop's",
    "manifest.webmanifest. Its own name, its own icon and its own scope, so a",
    "phone that has both keeps them apart — and so installing ops never puts a",
    "shop icon on a staff member's home screen.",
    "",
    "The scope is the string /ops, which prefix-matches ops.html, ops-login.html,",
    "ops-category.html and ops-reset.html. Everything else on the domain opens in",
    "the browser, which is right: a link to a product belongs in the shop."
  ],
  "id": "/ops.html",
  "name": "Rex-Giddoty Ops",
  "short_name": "Ops",
  "description": "Operations console for Rex-Giddoty Hubs — products, orders, customers and support.",
  "start_url": "/ops.html",
  "scope": "/ops",
  "display": "standalone",
  "orientation": "any",
  "background_color": "#2f2f35",
  "theme_color": "#0c0c0d",
  "categories": [
    "business",
    "productivity"
  ],
  "icons": [
    {
      "src": "/assets/ops-icon-192.png",
      "sizes": "192x192",
      "type": "image/png",
      "purpose": "any"
    },
    {
      "src": "/assets/ops-icon-512.png",
      "sizes": "512x512",
      "type": "image/png",
      "purpose": "any"
    },
    {
      "src": "/assets/ops-icon-maskable-512.png",
      "sizes": "512x512",
      "type": "image/png",
      "purpose": "maskable"
    }
  ]
}
